{"metadata":{"fragments":[{"text":"actor","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BufferingResource","kind":"identifier"}],"externalID":"s:13ReadiumShared17BufferingResourceC","roleHeading":"Class","symbolKind":"class","modules":[{"name":"ReadiumShared"}],"role":"symbol","title":"BufferingResource","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"BufferingResource","kind":"identifier"}]},"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["iOS"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"actor"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"BufferingResource"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Expensive interaction with the underlying resource is minimized, since most","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(smaller) requests can be satisfied by accessing the buffer alone. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"drawback is that some extra space is required to hold the buffer and that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"copying takes place when filling that buffer, but this is usually","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"outweighed by the performance benefits.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Note that this implementation is pretty limited and the benefits are only","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"apparent when reading forward and consecutively – e.g. when downloading the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"resource by chunks. The buffer is ignored when reading backward or far","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ahead.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/readiumshared\/bufferingresource"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Initializers","a